{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170487-zombie-lords","id":170487,"title":"Zombie Lords","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-16T00:50:11-07:00","id":170487,"title":"Zombie Lords","content":"A suggestion I think I made on the old forums even before Geist came out that I think, while generic in principle I think they'd make more sense to show up most in geist, thematically.<br /> <br /> Typhoid Maries, the contaminated, necromancers, they are people who have made the transition from normal person to a living lord of zombies.<br /> <br /> Just as zombies can happen through science, ritual, or cursed places, so can zombie lords. <br /> <br /> A school teacher is bitten in the same uprising that killed her family, she didn't die, but now she can feel the zombies in her mind, and tell them what to do.<br /> <br /> A roving band of werewolves attack a small town only to discover that the undertaker has prepared the occupants of every grave to defend the living, something he learned to do as a priest who buried Pharaohs in his day.<br /> <br /> A soup kitchen cook in an urban blight discovers that the horrors of violence and death causes those who die to rise up, and that his very soul has been contaminated as well, and now he still cares for his charges, the living and the dead.<br /> <br /> Whether the first zombie lord was a necromancer transformed by their rituals or just someone unlucky enough to be in a cursed spot long enough for them to be changed by the cursed land no one can know, the infected tend to be a newer phenomena, but there are rumours of typhoid maries who predate the modern era.<br /> <br /> The powers of zombie lords are the same as their charges: aspects.<br /> <br /> Some zombie lords are immortal enough to neither age, and if decapitated they just need one of their charges to staple their heads back to their neck, others have an evil eye that allows them to turn someone into a zombie by an act of will, some are highly resistant to all forms of magic, etc, etc. <br /> <br /> I figure sin-eaters would view zombie lords with caution, unlike abmortals there is nothing innately predatory about their nature, but any individual that could potentially unleash a zombie apocalypse is something they're going to want to keep an eye on. <br /> <br /> Better name suggestions are welcome, as are suggestions for more exotic types than equivalents of the three major types of zombies from antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T06:30:55-07:00","id":170667,"title":"","content":"Mummy: The Curse has an Utterance (Words of Dead Glory, from memory) that creates a revenant with an infectious bite, as well as access to ghost numina. Could work pretty well as a base for this type of creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T23:18:56-07:00","id":171437,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I wish they would publish sorcerer rules for mummy finally, a sorcerer zombie lord sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T10:03:18-07:00","id":178043,"title":"","content":"Oooh, I'm liking this idea! Maybe Sin-Eaters get involved because one zombie lord (you could call it a <i>Necrourge,</i> a slightly more literal term for &quot;mage of the dead&quot; than Necromancer) creates his servants by forcing a soul out of its body, then briefly channeling his own into it. This could either create a ghost (who is understandably not happy that his body is still walking around animated when he's not inside it) or be one more factor that pisses off a recently created ghost and drives it to destructive actions that draw the eyes of the player characters.<br /> $0.02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T15:59:16-07:00","id":178377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170487-zombie-lords?p=171437#post171437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, I wish they would publish sorcerer rules for mummy finally, a sorcerer zombie lord sounds interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming there are sorcerer rules. Have they ever actually promised such or is that just really big fan thing?(don't get me wrong, I am one such fan)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T16:59:56-07:00","id":178426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170487-zombie-lords?p=178377#post178377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming there are sorcerer rules. Have they ever actually promised such or is that just really big fan thing?(don't get me wrong, I am one such fan)</div> </div> </div> </div>The really cheap way would simply direct people to Second Sight. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T17:05:30-07:00","id":178430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170487-zombie-lords?p=178377#post178377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming there are sorcerer rules. Have they ever actually promised such or is that just really big fan thing?(don't get me wrong, I am one such fan)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a table on page 86 of Guildhalls of the Deathless with a category labelled &quot;Supernatural Beings (Including Mortal Sorcerers)&quot;. Probably the only real definitive time they've been mentioned in a rule section rather than the fluff. Given what we know about the Deceived, however, it seems like it would be a natural thing for some mortals to have similar powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T17:48:18-07:00","id":178460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170487-zombie-lords?p=178426#post178426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The really cheap way would simply direct people to Second Sight. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of sounding like a smartass, they <i>did</i> just port a bunch of the kludge Numina for revenants from Antagonists wholesale. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T07:59:53-07:00","id":178933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170487-zombie-lords?p=178426#post178426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The really cheap way would simply direct people to Second Sight. :P</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really, since it seems reasonable to assume that the sorcerers are among those creating relics in the modern day, and can apparently teach mummies rituals.<br /> <br /> Since relic creation isn't a thing in second sight, the default rules assumption is that thaumaturges don't have tricks up their sleeves as awesome as mummy rituals, and thaumaturge is limited by one's magical tradition, so you'd have to make up a proto-egyptian tradition with merits at least similar enough to mummy rituals that it makes sense that a thaumaturge can teach a mummy one of their tricks.<br /> <br /> In which case you've got something that looks pretty much nothing like the thaumaturges from Second Sight anyway, so that seems like a lot of bother.<br /> <br /> I'd kludge them by using the sorcery rules from Mirrors and adding the relic maker merit from Reliquary, far less trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}